344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (We are honoured to serve in the faculty of the Executive Board for the duration of this simulation of the United Nations Human Rights Council at DPSHMUN 2026. The Human Rights Council was established by Resolution 60/251 of the General Assembly and plays an integral part in the international human rights movement, as it is the primary intergovernmental body within the United Nations that deals with the issue of safeguarding human rights. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (This Background Guide has been meticulously crafted to catalyze furthering your research, and we hope that after perusing this guide, you will be well equipped to delve into the intricacies of the Human Rights Council, and specifically the complexities of our agenda. Keep in mind that this Background Guide is in no way exhaustive in nature, and is only intended to provide an elementary understanding of the agenda at hand. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 303 0 R
/E (In addition to this, we would like to stress that while this Guide may prompt you in a certain direction, by no means does that validate nor does it refute that perspective, and thus, we emphasise delegates doing extensive research into their foreign policies. While new ideas are inherently disruptive, they are far less disruptive than a world dominated by stereotypes and regional instability. We urge delegates to consider this while brainstorming ideas for sustained improvement in human rights, and not to refrain from proposing innovative solutions, whether temporary or permanent, out of fear of being too disruptive. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
