/P 321 0 R
/T (The conflict is a century-long dispute over land, sovereignty, and national identity in the Levant. It traces its modern roots to the late 19th-century rise of Zionism and the subsequent British Mandate for Palestine. The 1947 UN Partition Plan \(Resolution 181\) proposed separate Jewish and Arab states, which led to the 1948 Arab-Israeli War, the establishment of Israel, and the displacement of over 700,000 Palestinians \(the Nakba\). Despite the 1993 Oslo Accords establishing the Palestinian Authority \(PA\) for limited self-governance, continuous settlement expansion, the blockade of Gaza since 2007, and the absence of a viable path to a two-state solution have entrenched a cycle of systemic violence, only escalating after the 7th October Hamas attacks. )
/E (The conflict is a century-long dispute over land, sovereignty, and national identity in the Levant. It traces its modern roots to the late 19th-century rise of Zionism and the subsequent British Mandate for Palestine. The 1947 UN Partition Plan \(Resolution 181\) proposed separate Jewish and Arab states, which led to the 1948 Arab-Israeli War, the establishment of Israel, and the displacement of over 700,000 Palestinians \(the Nakba\). Despite the 1993 Oslo Accords establishing the Palestinian Authority \(PA\) for limited self-governance, continuous settlement expansion, the blockade of Gaza since 2007, and the absence of a viable path to a two-state solution have entrenched a cycle of systemic violence, only escalating after the 7th October Hamas attacks. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
665 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 321 0 R
/T (Over 80% of Gaza's housing, water sanitation networks, and electrical grids have been systematically leveled or deactivated. Critical shortages of anesthetics, antibiotics, and clean water have crippled the remaining functional hospitals, leaving thousands of chronic and trauma patients without care. In the West Bank, forced evictions, punitive home demolitions, and expanding illegal settlements have displaced thousands of Palestinians, fueled by armed settler excursions. )
/E (Over 80% of Gaza's housing, water sanitation networks, and electrical grids have been systematically leveled or deactivated. Critical shortages of anesthetics, antibiotics, and clean water have crippled the remaining functional hospitals, leaving thousands of chronic and trauma patients without care. In the West Bank, forced evictions, punitive home demolitions, and expanding illegal settlements have displaced thousands of Palestinians, fueled by armed settler excursions. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
