/E (Following the collapse of the Assad regime, Syria is undergoing a precarious political transition. While the transitional government in Damascus attempts to present a moderate, inclusive platform to secure international recognition, deep structural fault lines remain. Tensions between Damascus and the Kurdish-led SDF over regional autonomy persist, while Turkish troops maintain a presence in the north, and Israeli forces enforce strict buffer zones in the south to prevent hostile elements from consolidating power. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
678 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 322 0 R
/E (AI application in Syria is defined by decentralized drone warfare and digital surveillance. Various factions utilize low-cost commercial drones modified with AI-enabled facial recognition and autonomous flight pathing to bypass electronic jamming. Additionally, the transitional government and local militias use automated social media monitoring algorithms to scan public platforms, track political dissidents, and map potential domestic opposition. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
