/S /H1
/P 324 0 R
/T (Red Sea  The conflict developed directly from the regional escalation of the Gaza war. In late 2023, the Houthi movement in Yemen declared its intention to target any commercial or military vessels in the Red Sea linked to Israel, or those bound for Israeli ports, as an act of solidarity with the Palestinian population. The Red Sea is an essential global maritime artery, carrying roughly 12% of international trade and 30% of global container traffic via the Bab al-Mandab Strait. The persistent attacks forced a major international maritime security crisis. )
/E (Red Sea  The conflict developed directly from the regional escalation of the Gaza war. In late 2023, the Houthi movement in Yemen declared its intention to target any commercial or military vessels in the Red Sea linked to Israel, or those bound for Israeli ports, as an act of solidarity with the Palestinian population. The Red Sea is an essential global maritime artery, carrying roughly 12% of international trade and 30% of global container traffic via the Bab al-Mandab Strait. The persistent attacks forced a major international maritime security crisis. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 324 0 R
/T (The Red Sea remains a contested naval combat zone. Despite continuous counter-strikes by US and British naval assets targeting Houthi radar installations, coastal launch pads, and underground storage facilities in western Yemen, the Houthis retain the capability to launch asymmetric strikes. Most major commercial shipping firms continue to avoid the Suez Canal route, opting for longer, more expensive alternative passages. )
/E (The Red Sea remains a contested naval combat zone. Despite continuous counter-strikes by US and British naval assets targeting Houthi radar installations, coastal launch pads, and underground storage facilities in western Yemen, the Houthis retain the capability to launch asymmetric strikes. Most major commercial shipping firms continue to avoid the Suez Canal route, opting for longer, more expensive alternative passages. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
