/Title (The Red Sea remains a contested naval combat zone. Despite continuous counter-strikes by US and British naval assets targeting Houthi radar installations, coastal launch pads, and underground storage facilities in western Yemen, the Houthis retain the capability to launch asymmetric strikes. Most major commercial shipping firms continue to avoid the Suez Canal route, opting for longer, more expensive alternative passages.)
